    gd: 'Well-worn and common — freelance branding work, running a small design studio, or building a personal client base is a realistic path once you have 3-4 strong projects to show.',
    uiux: 'Realistic but requires a wider skill set to sell solo — freelance and consulting UI/UX work exists and pays well per hour, but it usually needs more years of in-house experience first to build credibility with clients who cannot easily judge research quality themselves.',
  },
];

const freelanceRows = [
  {
    aspect: 'Typical India hourly rate',
    gd: 'Roughly Rs 500-1,500/hour for freshers and mid-level freelancers, rising toward Rs 2,500-3,000/hour for experienced brand and packaging specialists.',
    uiux: 'Roughly Rs 2,500-7,000/hour for experienced freelancers, reflecting the narrower pool of designers who can credibly run research and deliver tested product screens, not just visuals.',
  },
  {
    aspect: 'How clients find and vet you',
    gd: 'Visually — a client can judge a graphic design portfolio in seconds, which makes cold outreach and marketplace listings (Fiverr, Behance, Instagram) a realistic acquisition channel.',
    uiux: 'Less visually, more by reputation and referral — a non-technical client often cannot judge whether your research methodology was sound, so trust usually comes through referrals, case studies, or a track record with similar products.',
  },
  {
    aspect: 'Repeat-client potential',
    gd: 'High for ongoing brand or marketing work — a business needs new social creatives, ads, and collateral constantly, which supports recurring freelance income.',
    uiux: 'Project-based and less naturally recurring — most products need a UI/UX overhaul or a defined feature project rather than continuous weekly design work, so freelance UI/UX income is often lumpier unless you build a retainer relationship.',
  },
  {
    aspect: 'Realistic first-client path',
    gd: 'A small business needing a logo, social kit, or one-off campaign is an easy, low-friction first client to find through marketplaces or local networks.',
    uiux: 'A startup founder needing a defined MVP screen set or a redesign sprint is a realistic first client, but usually requires a stronger portfolio and a warmer introduction than graphic design freelancing does.',
