  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Biology',
    body: 'Graphic design rewards people who want a fast, tangible creative win and are energised by producing a finished visual object. UI/UX rewards people who are comfortable with a slower, evidence-based cycle where the design is only "done" after real users have tested it. Both need genuine visual sense — the difference is whether your satisfaction comes from the finished look or from the proof that it works.',
    note: 'If watching a user struggle with your design feels like a personal insult rather than useful data, that discomfort is a real signal worth taking seriously before you commit to UX.',
  },
  {
