    title: 'Context',
    body: 'Can your family runway absorb a fresher-level salary (Rs 2-4 LPA for graphic design, Rs 2.5-7 LPA for UI/UX) for the first 1-2 years while you build real proof? Graphic design proof can be built faster and cheaper with personal projects; UI/UX proof needs at least a handful of willing test users, which takes more coordination even if it costs nothing.',
    note: 'If you have zero access to real users to test with, start with lightweight guerrilla testing on friends and family rather than waiting for a "proper" research setup that never arrives.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Market',
    body: 'Graphic design has broad, steady demand but a comparatively low entry bar, which means high competition and price pressure at the entry level. UI/UX has narrower, more specialised demand concentrated in tech, SaaS, and product companies, but with fewer qualified candidates competing for each opening.',
